# Sentinel build context filter (SPEC-P16 §1).
#
# Keep the docker build context small and secret-free. The image must never
# contain `.env` or runtime state; `docs/backtest-report.json` DOES stay in
# context (the runtime image ships it for the dashboard's backtest panel) —
# only `docs/evidence` is excluded.

# --- Rust build artifacts & VCS -------------------------------------------
target/
.git/

# --- Runtime state (host-side journal / breaker state / logs) -------------
data/
logs/

# --- Node trees (indexer + CRE workflow are not part of the docker image) --
**/node_modules/
indexer/
workflow-cre/node_modules/
workflow-cre/target/
workflow-cre/dist/

# --- Vendored reference repos (re-clone via scripts/verify-facts.sh) ------
vendor/

# --- Foundry build output (not needed by the Rust workspace) --------------
contracts/out/
contracts/cache/

# --- Evidence dumps (keep docs/backtest-report.json) ----------------------
docs/evidence/

# --- Secrets: never send `.env` to the daemon (placeholders exempt) -------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
